@itsbreepayne A Pastel de Belém and a Pastel de Nata are essentially the same type of Portuguese custard tart. The difference is that “Pastel de Belém” is the name used exclusively by the famous bakery in Belém, Lisbon, where the original recipe was created in the 19th century. Their recipe is a closely guarded secret.

“Pastel de Nata” is the generic name for the same pastry made everywhere else in Portugal and around the world. While recipes may vary slightly from bakery to bakery, they are all inspired by the original Pastel de Belém.

In short: every Pastel de Belém is a Pastel de Nata, but not every Pastel de Nata is a Pastel de Belém. 🇵🇹🥧

